{
  "case_id": "2024-24a884",
  "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:12 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On January 20, 2025, President Trump issued Executive Order 14,160, Protecting the Meaning and Value of American Citizenship."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Applicants",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Universal injunctions exceed the judicial power granted in Article III, which exists only to address the injury to the complaining party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 7
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: General Sauer, the -- these universal injunctions, as you say, have proliferated over the last three decades or so. Would you discuss, though, the origins of universal injunctions?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry. CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: You -- JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Here -- CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Go ahead. JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Here, there's a discrete identified group on one issue: Does citizenship mean are you born in the territory of the United States, or does it mean are you loyal to someone else, which is your claim, or are your parents loyal to someone else?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GORSUCH",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, what -- what do you say, though, to the suggestion, General, that in this particular case, those patchwork problems for, frankly, the government, as -- as well as for plaintiffs, justify broader relief?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General SAUER",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Rule 23 provides the equitable tools subject to rigorous criteria, appropriately rigorous criteria, to obtain that kind of class-wide and emergency relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice THOMAS",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General, when were the first universal injunctions used?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General SAUER",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the point is that universal injunctions exceed traditional principles of Article III and they exceed the traditional equitable authority and that's what yields all these sort of pathologies, so to speak, of the current practice of issuing them very, very easily."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You claim that there is absolutely no constitutional way to stop --put this aside -- to stop a president from an unconstitutional act, a clearly, indisputably unconstitutional act, taking every gun from every citizen, we"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Congress",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "some people in Congress who argued against the Thirteenth Amendment just because of that, some people who argued against passing the amendment just because of that, because it would give citizenship to gypsies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the relevant history of the Fourteenth Amendment is the statements of Senator Trumbull, who emphasized that domicile was the key criteria, and he said that in a letter to Andrew Jackson"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, General, on this question of expedition, I mean, it -- it sort of depends on the government's own actions in a case like this one, where one can expect that there is not going to be a great deal of disagreement among the lower courts."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "U.S. Government",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our general practice is to respect those precedents, but there are circumstances when it is not a categorical practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: But the government's done that in other cases too, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Alito asked you, well, what's -- what's the point of this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. Mr. Feigenbaum."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeremy M. Feigenbaum (amicus)",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0003-0005",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGENBAUM: So I do feel like something of an amicus to this question because nothing in my injunction rises or falls on this claim bucket."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You don't get to squiggle out into the first bucket, okay? We're in the third bucket."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "States",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "-- which is I think it requires having district courts consider the availability of the alternative and explaining why it's not workable in the case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigenbaum",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 91,
        "start": 91
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "States can't represent those individuals in class actions, nor would we try to. They can't represent us and you don't have classes of states. So the whole framework doesn't apply to state litigation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ARE -- are you telling us that we really can't decide the question that we asked to have briefing and argument on without taking a -- a peek at the merits?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigenbaum",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 98,
        "start": 98
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And so I do think we have pretty significant pocketbook injuries like in Nebraska to the tunes of millions of dollars, and whether we get those remedies or don't get those remedied is going to turn on the merits, is going to turn on the nature of the harms, and then, ultimately, the workability of the alternatives."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0004-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 102,
        "start": 102
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you agree with me that they were not presented to the courts below?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amici",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 108,
        "start": 108
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "one of our amici points out to them, the Pierce versus Society of Sisters case, the West Virginia State Board of Education case, those were earlier than the 1960s."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Kelsi B. Corkran",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 126,
        "start": 126
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The executive order's stripping of citizenship from U.S.-born children is contrary not only to the Fourteenth Amendment's plain text but also our common law history, this Court's precedent, a federal statute, and over a century of executive branch practice."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0005-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 128,
        "start": 128
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: You say the government is wrong about the availability of preliminary injunctions. On what do you base that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So I -- you know, again, I would put us in the complete relief bucket. So I'll -- like Mr. Feigenbaum, I'll put on my amici hat in answering that question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 129,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I understand General Sauer's proposal to be that we channel all of this through Rule 23."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0006-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 130,
        "start": 129
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why can't you get putative class relief in a preliminary injunction or TRO posture?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 151,
        "start": 151
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Kavanaugh: Some of your concerns about this Court being involved, I guess I'm not sure I really understand that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Sauer",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 152,
        "start": 152
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "General Sauer's point that this has become pathological in the number of universal injunctions that are making its way onto the Court's emergency docket, but my --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Corkran",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 152,
        "start": 152
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I would say first that the government, I think, pretty dramatically overstates them. It's double-counting TROs and PIs in the same case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 156,
        "start": 156
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they're not really, I thought, getting relief."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor Pfander",
      "case_id": "2024-24a884",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f96a441c2d484a57cd3055a83ddee3cda1c55c285ecfb99b57c629f5caecbe76",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f96a441c2d48-0007-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 157,
        "start": 157
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think Professor Pfander's amicus brief is really helpful on that."
    },
